{#- Client side of formulas/healthchecks: a tiny helper other formulas' jobs
   call to ping a check by slug (auto-created on first ping, ?create=1).

   base_url: the Healthchecks instance (its site_root).
   ping_key: the project's ping key (Project Settings -> Ping key), from
   OpenBao. Optional: empty or unresolved = `enabled` False — the helper
   and its key file are removed, and consumers (formulas/backup,
   formulas/salt-minion) render no ping at all. Pings are a convenience
   signal, never a reason for a job or a state run to fail.

   script: `hc-ping <slug> <status>` — status 0 (success), fail, an exit
   code, or `systemd` (from $SERVICE_RESULT in an ExecStopPost). It returns
   at once: the curl runs in a transient systemd unit (systemd-run), so a
   slow or down Healthchecks never delays or fails the job. curl retries
   every retry_delay seconds for up to retry_max_time — long enough to ride
   out Healthchecks' own nightly backup stop on jellyfin.
   env_file: root-only, holds the ping URL (base_url/ping/<key>). #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'base_url': '',
    'ping_key': '',
    'pkg': 'curl',
    'curl_bin': '/usr/bin/curl',
    'systemd_run_bin': '/usr/bin/systemd-run',
    'script': '/usr/local/sbin/hc-ping',
    'config_dir': '/etc/healthchecks-ping',
    'env_file': '/etc/healthchecks-ping/env',
    'max_time': 10,
    'retry_delay': 15,
    'retry_max_time': 300,
} %}
{%- set hc_ping = salt['pillar.get']('healthchecks_ping:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
{%- set _key = hc_ping.ping_key %}
{%- do hc_ping.update({'enabled': (hc_ping.base_url | length > 0 and _key is string
                                   and _key | length > 0 and not _key.startswith('sdb://'))}) %}
